+    // The four libsd routines above, generic over the machine they run on. Regs has gpr[32], hi
+    // and lo; Bus has lw(address) for RAM and io16(address, index) / io16(address, value, index)
+    // for the routine's one register access per half word, index = how many instructions of the
+    // caller's sequence (base + the routine's own) ran before it, i.e. the IOP cycle it happens
+    // at relative to the caller's start. Returns the instructions the guest routine executes.
+    template <class Regs, class Bus>
